# Build-context exclusions. The release job checks out clean, so this mostly
# matters for a local `podman build` against a working tree — where `target/`
# alone is tens of gigabytes and would be streamed to the engine before the
# first instruction ran, for files the Containerfile never COPYs.
target/
crates/*/dist/
data/
end2end/test-results/
node_modules/
.git/
